    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d467">

                <pb facs="0564" n="554" sameAs="frus:frus1944v02/pg554"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.796/10–644: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-10-06T17:00:00+01:00">October 6, 1944—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 6—2:52 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>8896. ReDepts 8104, October 4, 1 p.m. The Foreign Office confirmed this morning
                    that paragraphs 3 and 4 of the British reply to the invitation to the
                    International Civil Aviation Conference were intended as a statement of the
                    British objectives and of the position which they will assume during the
                    Conference.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
